{
    desc => ':set theme=light switches from dark to light theme',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/set_theme_light`

Tests that `:set theme=light` applies the light color scheme at runtime,
changing the editor background to a light tone and adjusting all foreground
and syntax colors for readability on a bright background.

Starts from the dark theme so the transition to light is clearly visible.

Ex: `:set theme=light`

- **set_theme_light_dark_initial.png**: Dark theme active with dark
  background and light text before the switch.
- **set_theme_light_applied.png**: Light theme active with light/warm
  background and dark text; syntax colors updated for the light palette.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->editor->set_theme('dark');
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('dark_initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->ex('set theme=light');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('applied');
    },
}
__DATA__
# Theme switch test
Hello, World!
my $x = 42;
print "light mode\n";
